  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OnUpdateFiberStackSize",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend.c",
    "description": "`OnUpdateFiberStackSize` accepts negative INI values via `zend_ini_parse_quantity_warn()` and stores them directly into `EG(fiber_stack_size)` (a `size_t`). With input `ini_set(\"fiber.stack_size\", \"-1\")`, this becomes a huge unsigned value. Later, `ZEND_METHOD(Fiber, start)` in `php-src/Zend/zend_fibers.c` passes this unchecked size to `zend_fiber_init_context()`, which computes `stack = pointer + size` and calls `make_fcontext()`. The wrapped/invalid stack top causes `make_fcontext` to write through an invalid address (crash at `make_x86_64_sysv_elf_gas.S:69`).",
    "conditions": "PoV sets `fiber.stack_size` to `-1` at runtime, creates a Fiber, then calls `Fiber->start()`. Data flow: user script `ini_set()` -> `OnUpdateFiberStackSize` sets `EG(fiber_stack_size)` without rejecting negative values -> `zim_Fiber_start`/`zend_fiber_init_context` uses that size for stack math -> invalid top-of-stack passed to `make_fcontext` -> wild write/SEGV."
  },
